course: dictionary
lesson: 5428
title: Lagoon: a calm pool beside the sea
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A lagoon is a stretch of water that is almost cut off from the sea. Read the words around it to find its meaning: «Venice in Italy is built on more than a hundred small islands in a lagoon.» Islands sit in water, so a lagoon is the water between them, not land.
explain: The sea is kept out by a sandbank, a reef or a strip of land. Think of a lagoon as a calm pool that the sea has partly walled off. Check your guess by swapping it into the sentence: «Grey whales have babies in warm lagoons in Mexico in winter» still makes sense if lagoon means a calm, sheltered stretch of water.
explain: The word can mean more than one thing. In a story, «the blue lagoon» is a calm, beautiful place on a tropical island. The calm water inside a ring-shaped coral island is a lagoon too. People can also make a lagoon, a pond to hold waste water. The clues in the sentence tell you which kind is meant.
fact: A lagoon is a stretch of water, often salty, that is separated from the sea.
fact: A sandbank, a reef or a strip of land can shut a lagoon off from the sea.
fact: «Lagoon» can also mean the calm water inside a coral atoll.
fact: «Lagoon» can also mean a pool made by people to hold waste water.
fact: Grey whales feed in the Arctic in summer and have babies in warm lagoons in Mexico in winter.
exercise: «Venice is built on more than a hundred small islands in a lagoon.» What is a lagoon here? | A long road over the sea | A tall hill covered in grass | *A stretch of water separated from the sea | A type of gondola
exercise: «Grey whales have babies in warm lagoons in Mexico in winter.» Find and copy one word that names a place where whales have babies. | winter | Mexico | whales | *lagoons
exercise: In a story, «the blue lagoon» is a calm, beautiful place. What kind of place is it? | A noisy, crowded town | A dark cave under the ground | A busy railway station | *A calm, beautiful place on a tropical island
test: Inside a ring-shaped coral island, the calm water is called a lagoon. What is that ring-shaped island called? | A canal | A gondola | *An atoll | A sandbank
test: Why might people make a lagoon? | *To hold waste water | To carry gondolas through a city | To make a road across the sea | To keep whales warm in winter
exam: «Venice was built on islands in a shallow lagoon at the top of the Adriatic Sea.» What is the lagoon? | A mountain range | *A shallow stretch of water near the sea | A desert of sand | A thick forest
